<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        Two example answers, built in Python rather than written out here.

        They have to go *after* whatever is already there, and the sequence
        they need therefore depends on what the shop has - an XML record would
        have to guess a number, and guessing low is the one mistake that
        matters here: a rule the bot tries early takes matches away from the
        ones below it, silently.

        One of the two is switched off, so that tab is not empty.

        The method does nothing once a demo answer exists, so a shop that has
        written its own never sprouts examples. The thirteen real answers in
        bot_rules.xml are left alone - those are the shop's own words, and they
        sit under noupdate for that reason.

        Not noupdate: with it the function would only run on a fresh install,
        and a shop upgrading into this feature would never see the examples.
        The method guards itself instead.
    -->
    <data>
        <function model="mart369.bot.rule" name="_mart369_load_bot_demo"/>
    </data>
</odoo>
